# Example: add this to the global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md on your multi-session host

Copy the section below into `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` on the machine that hosts
your Claude Code sessions/slots. Claude Code loads that file automatically
into every session for that user, so any slot that starts up will know
`hub-tell` exists without you having to explain it each time.

---

## Messaging between sessions on this host

If you need to notify or ask something of ANOTHER Claude Code session
running on this same machine (e.g. "let the deploy session know X is
live"), use:

    hub-tell <session-name> "<message>"

Example: `hub-tell backend "Deploy finished, please check the logs"`.

- `<session-name>` is the short name (without the `slot-` prefix), e.g.
  `backend`, `docs`, `01`.
- The message arrives as a normal user turn in that session's conversation,
  prefixed with `[hub-tell from <your-session>]` so it knows where it came
  from.
- If the target session doesn't exist (not open), `hub-tell` fails with a
  clear error instead of doing nothing silently.
- This only works for sessions on THIS machine - it does not reach other
  hosts, other operating systems, or unrelated Claude Code clients.
